# Project Tools

These tools cover project-wide editor operations and reusable content validation helpers.

## Tools

- `create_input_mapping(action_name, key, input_type="Action")`
  - Adds an input mapping to project settings.
- `audit_content_root_mcp(root_path, recursive=true, scan_paths=true, include_dependencies=true, include_assets=false, write_report=false, forbidden_dependency_prefixes=None, required_asset_paths=None, expected_asset_count=None, expected_class_counts=None, max_samples=50, fail_on_dirty_packages=false, fail_on_redirectors=true, fail_on_forbidden_dependencies=true)`
  - Read-only audit for a `/Game` content root.
- `recreate_content_folder_mcp(...)`
  - Recreates a source content folder into a target folder using the MCP reusable-content pipeline.
- `postprocess_content_folder_mcp(...)`
  - Runs the postprocess/reference repair phase against an already-created target folder.
- `repair_world_actor_instances_mcp(map_path, source_root="/Game/UltraDynamicSky", target_root="/Game/_MCP_Temp/UltraDynamicSky_MCP", suffix="_MCP", dry_run=false, save_map=true, remap_level_blueprint=false, repair_actor_classes=true, repair_component_classes=true, remap_actor_references=true, remove_source_object_map_keys=true, check_editor_log_health=true, fail_on_editor_log_issues=true, suppress_editor_prompts=true)`
  - Repairs actor/component instances and object-key maps in one explicit target map.
- `replace_asset_references_mcp(replacements=None, target_root="", target_paths=None, source_root="", string_replacements=None, name_replacements=None, dry_run=true, save_assets=false, scan_paths=true, refresh_materials=true, include_package_objects=false, allow_non_game_targets=false)`
  - Replaces object references plus path-like text/name references in target assets.
  - Defaults are non-mutating and project-scoped: `dry_run=true`, `save_assets=false`, `include_package_objects=false`, and explicit `target_paths` must be under `/Game`.
  - `string_replacements` or `name_replacements` can be used without object `replacements` for tightly scoped text-only repair.
  - Pass `dry_run=false` only after reviewing the replacement report.
- `analyze_blueprint_widget_fallbacks_mcp(source_root, target_root, suffix="_MCP")`
  - Checks whether recreated Blueprint/Widget assets still need duplicate fallback handling.
- `create_volume_texture_from_2d_sheet_mcp(...)`
  - Creates or updates a `VolumeTexture` from a tiled `Texture2D`.
- `create_volume_texture_from_raw_rgba16_sheet_mcp(...)`
  - Creates or updates a `Texture2D` and `VolumeTexture` from a raw RGBA16 sheet.
- `set_material_texture_sample_sampler_type_mcp(material_path, texture_path, sampler_type="SAMPLERTYPE_LinearColor", dry_run=false, save=true, compile=true)`
  - Changes sampler type on material `TextureSample` nodes referencing a texture.
- `run_content_validation_pipeline_mcp(...)`
  - Runs recreate, postprocess, optional world repair, and verification as one pipeline.

## Safety Rules

- Treat these as editor authoring helpers only. Finished project content must not gain an UnrealMCP dependency.
- `replace_asset_references_mcp` rejects MCP-only replacement targets, is dry-run by default, and refuses non-`/Game` target assets unless `allow_non_game_targets=true` is explicit.
- Prefer explicit `target_paths` for narrow reference repairs; use `target_root` only after reviewing the affected asset set.
